@flotsam.festival 2026 🩵it was a pleasure to document the amazing festival throughout May

2 (and a bit) jam-packed weeks of Flotsam across the southern Gold Coast - workshops, pop-ups, exhibitions, and talks celebrating surf media culture, spread across galleries, beach parks, and community spaces, despite whatever the weather threw at us. 

A few years ago, I went to a few of the workshops, came out insanely inspired to push myself more with water photography and it helped connect me with people who are some of my closest friends now. Feel very privileged to have been involved in this year’s one, full circle. Always so blown away by the insane talent

Events like this matter now more than ever. They give creatives a platform to showcase their work, meet each other, collaborate, and get inspired. 

It’s been amazing to watch Flotsam grow over the years and see the impact it continues to have on the local creative community. A huge thank you to Carolyn for creating and nurturing something that celebrates creativity and genuinely supports local artists, photographers, filmmakers, and storytellers.

