Most regular photography exhibitions have a launch party. Luckily, Canisters isn't your regular photography exhibition. 

Flotsam's group analogue photography experiment Canisters will host a closing party at @ironandresingarage

Featuring:
@ryanheywood
@tania_film
@mikecalvino
@lucasgardnerphoto
@claudiasajeva
Plus international submissions from @lomography worldwide, including @martynaskatauskas @jeancric @pedro.pinxit @lomogocchin @szumi_ziarno

For the closing event, the exhibition flips into a one-night-only art lottery. Your “ticket” is an empty film canister, each one hiding a number that matches a fine art print on the wall. Limited 6 x 8 inch collectible prints from featured artists or full size works are up for grabs.

No one knows what they’ll get, old school style: just like the thrill of waiting for film to develop.

Proceeds from every canister sold goes directly to featured artists, with a few extra surprise prizes in the mix: think film processing vouchers, reloaded cameras, and everything you need to kickstart your own analogue obsession.

With the fine folk at @bayou_film and @wadesworld_photographics + more loading up the prize pool, swing by to enjoy food, drinks, tunes and seriously good film.

Exhibition: daily until 14th May Iron & Resin
Closing party: 14th May, 5.30 PM onwards 

Come for the art. Leave with a piece of it.

